The best interval we can use (the interval whose points are given that's closest to $x=2$) is the interval between $x=1$ and $x=4$. Let's find the average rate of change between those points.

$\begin{align}
f'(2)&\approx\dfrac{f(4)-f(1)}{4-1}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{-33-(-25)}{3}
\\\\
&\approx-2.67
\end{align}$
